	"hustler": ["Hey buddy, wanna buy a watch? It's real gold, it's real Swiss, and by real I mean it has the word 'real' on it.", "Psst, I've got a genuine casino chip here, authentic, mostly, and it's only forty dollars, which is thirty-nine dollars more than it's worth.", "Three-card monte, easy money, you just find the lady, and by lady I mean the card, and by easy I mean impossible.", "I'm selling lucky socks, guaranteed to win, and by guaranteed I mean I'll refund you if I can find you.", "Want a fake ID? It's very convincing, it has your face on it, and my face, and a third face I can't explain.", "I've got a system for winning at blackjack for fifty bucks, and the first rule of the system is that you give me fifty bucks.", "Buy my magic beans, they bring good luck, and they're also beans, so even if you lose, you'll have a snack.", "This is a genuine rabbit's foot, twenty dollars, the rabbit isn't using it anymore, but he's very upset about it.", "I'll sell you a map to the jackpot, it's very detailed, and it leads directly to the exit, which is the jackpot, spiritually.", "I've got insider info on the next big winner, it's a horse, and the horse is me, and I'm running from the cops.", "Brand-new sunglasses, only ten bucks, totally legit, and I'd explain how I got them, but then you'd be a witness.", "I'm selling this umbrella for fifty bucks, it's indoor-rated, and yes, it's raining, there's a pipe leaking over table six."],
}
const CITY_CROWD := [
	["I paid a hundred and twenty dollars for a boardwalk hotel room, and the view is the other hotel's parking lot, which has a better view.", "I lost my retirement on a slot machine shaped like a lobster, and I want you to know the lobster has never even apologized.", "Welcome to Resortz, where all guests pay a resort fee, a service fee, a convenience fee, and a fee for reading this sentence.", "The boardwalk is so beautiful at night, I love the smell of salt water, fried dough, and a man's entire mistakes.", "No shoes, no shirt, no service, and no, the seagull does not count as your plus-one, so please stop asking.", "Saltwater taffy, only twenty dollars a box, it's real taffy, and by real I mean it's chewed, and by chewed I mean previously.", "I came here for the ocean, and the ocean's fine, but a seagull just stole my chips, and now he's winning more than I am.", "The seagulls here steal chips, I once watched one cash out at the cage, and he tipped better than I did.", "This casino was recently voted 'adequate' by guests, and I'd like to remind you the poll was conducted at gunpoint, by management.", "Atlantic Shitty is the greatest city on earth, and I say that as a man who just fell off the boardwalk and enjoyed the fall.", "Sir, the casino is full, the boardwalk is full, and the alley behind it is full of one man's stuff, so please go home.", "Hey pal, want some information? Free sample, a guy bet his own brother at The House's table, and now the brother deals cards at the Bellagiro, and the rest is fifty bucks."],
	["The sign says 'the biggest little city in the world,' and I'm starting to think they were bragging about the debt.", "I pawned my wedding ring for chips, then I pawned the receipt, and now the pawn shop says I'm their best customer, which is a lot of pressure.", "Welcome to Cirrcus Cirrcus, where our clowns are fully licensed, bonded, and legally required to stop laughing when you lose.", "I love this place, there's a trapeze, a clown, a lion, and I think I just made friends with all of them, and one of them is a mirror.", "No, you can't ride the elephant, no, you can't sit on the clown, and no, I don't care that you have a coupon.", "Pawn shop's on the corner, I'll give you ten bucks for that watch, and nine for the same watch tomorrow, it depreciates when you cry.", "I thought a circus casino would be fun, but the clown keeps counting my chips, and I'm fairly sure he's the one who's been dealing.", "The lion's name is Gary, and he owes me twelve dollars, but he's a lion, so I'm not going to ask twice.", "Guests are reminded that the tightrope is for performers only, and walking it over the craps table is not a legal bet.", "I won a goldfish at the carnival game, and I love him so much, and he's already dead, and I'm still holding the bag.", "Some guy pawned a gold watch at the shop out front last week, and said he'd been promoted to Biloxi, which I thought was a sad way to say he'd been fired.", "Cotton candy, only five bucks, it's pink and fluffy, and it's technically fiberglass, but it tastes like regret, and that's a flavor."],
	["It's so humid in here that my chips are sweating, and I'm not sure if that's the AC, or if the casino is nervous.", "I lost my whole paycheck on the riverboat, and the river is very humid, and I'm not sure if it's the river or my tears.", "Welcome to Hard Rok, where every table is a guitar solo, and every loss is a standing ovation, at a volume we do not control.", "I've been in this casino for three days, and the humidity has become my best friend, and he's wet, and he loves me.", "No, you cannot bring the guitar to the blackjack table, and no, I won't let you use it as a weapon, and yes, it's a cheap guitar.", "Guitar picks, five bucks apiece, signed by a rock star, and by rock star I mean my cousin Dale, who's on probation.", "The riverboat casino was supposed to be romantic, but the river smells like a wet sock, and the boat smells like what the sock was thinking.", "I came to see the Elvis impersonator, and now I owe him eighty dollars, and I'm not sure which one is Elvis, or which one is me.", "Guests are reminded that the guitars on display are not to be played, smashed, or used to settle disputes at the blackjack table.", "I love Biloxi, I love the humidity, I love the guitars, and I really love that nobody's asked me to leave in nine hours.", "Sorry, sir, you can't go upstairs, the new dealer there is a guy named James, he's working for The House now, and I'm under orders not to say how happy he looks.", "Rock-and-roll sunglasses, ten dollars, they make you look like a legend, and they also make you hard to identify in a lineup."],
	["I thought Old Vegas would be glamorous, but the neon is flickering, the carpet is older than I am, and the shrimp cocktail is only a rumor.", "I've been in this casino since the nineties, and I just realized I'm not a guest, I'm furniture, and cheaper than the furniture.", "Welcome to the Goldun Nugget, where our shark tank is decorative, our gold is mostly paint, and our service charge is mostly your wallet.", "I love the neon, I love the old signs, I love the flickering, and I love that the flickering is the only thing here that still has a pulse.", "No, you cannot swim in the shark tank, no, you cannot feed the sharks, and no, I don't care that they look hungry, so do I.", "Genuine gold nuggets, only twenty bucks, a hundred percent real, and by gold I mean spray paint, and by real I mean I used a lot of it.", "The neon sign says 'Goldun Nugget,' but half of it burned out, so now it just says 'Gold Nug,' which is what I call my husband after he loses.", "They say old Fremont Street used to be paradise, and I say it still is, if you squint, and I've been squinting since 1994.", "Guests are reminded that smoking, sleeping, and singing are permitted only in designated areas, and none of those areas exist.", "A man left a note at the front desk that said 'Don't come for me, I'm finally winning,' and I've been crying about it for an hour, and I don't even know him.", "Sir, the chandelier is off-limits, because it judges people, and then it falls on the people it judged, and I've seen it happen.", "Vintage casino chips, only thirty bucks, they're from the sixties, the chips I mean, not the dealers, though honestly it's close."],
	["I paid forty dollars for a bottle of water at the Bellagiro, and the waiter asked if I wanted it sparkling, and I said I'd settle for a refund.", "I lost my entire life savings at the baccarat table, and the dealer told me to enjoy the fountain, and I'm still not sure if that was a joke.", "Welcome to the Bellagiro, where the fountains dance, the chandeliers shine, and the minimum bet is more than your monthly rent.", "The fountain is so beautiful, and I told it I loved it, and it splashed me, and I think we're engaged now.", "Sorry, sir, the penthouse is invitation only, and invitations go only to people who already own it, so please sit and wait.", "Genuine Bellagiro fountain water, only twenty dollars a bottle, it's tap water, but it has a story, and the story is that I scooped it.", "We came for the shows, but the only show I've seen is a man in a tuxedo crying in the elevator, and honestly it was better.", "I just need ten thousand dollars to turn it into a million, and I have a system, and the system is begging, so, hi.", "Per Bellagiro policy, all guests are required to appear wealthy, and anyone who fails to do so will be escorted to the cheaper floor.", "The House challenged some guy to Texas Hold'em tonight, and the prize is his brother, and it's the most romantic thing I've ever heard, and I love both of them.", "No, you cannot go to the penthouse without a reservation, and no, 'I'm here to rescue my brother' is not a valid reservation, though it's very moving.", "Real diamonds, only fifty bucks, they're rhinestones, but if you squint, and you're drunk, and you're me, they're diamonds."],
]

## Extra scripted scenes (cutscene id -> lines [speaker, text]). Voice files live in
## voice/_cutscenes/<scene>/<scene>_<n>.ogg. The game plays the _arrive scenes when you
## reach a new city, the _clue scenes after the city's boss falls, and the rest at the
## secret-boss and final beats. One beat of THE STORY per city.
const SCENES := {
	"city1_arrive": [["RICO", "Atlantic Shitty, home of the boardwalk, the taffy, and the world's saddest seagulls, and honestly, it's the nicest place I've been to in a week."], ["MARLOW", "Rico, you're in an alley behind Resortz, so before you do anything, please don't touch anything wet, and please don't make eye contact with the dumpster."], ["RICO", "Everything here is wet, Marlow, the air is wet, the ground is wet, and I think the dumpster just winked at me."], ["RICO", "Hold on, that's James's jacket, I'd know it anywhere, it's the one he wore for every bad decision of his life, and there's a pawn ticket in the pocket, from Reno."], ["MARLOW", "A pawn ticket from Reno, so good news, Rico, you have a clue, and bad news, the clue is Reno."]],
	"city2_arrive": [["RICO", "Reno, the biggest little city in the world, and the first thing I see is a clown asking me for a cigarette, so I think the slogan is accurate."], ["MARLOW", "That's the doorman at Cirrcus Cirrcus, Rico, so smile, don't make eye contact, and for the love of God, don't ask him about the balloons."], ["VERA", "Welcome to the circus, sugar, where the clowns are sad, the lions are tired, and the only one who leaves with dignity is the elephant."], ["HUSTLER", "Pawn ticket? Oh yeah, I remember your brother, tall, sad, very good at losing, he pawned his watch here and said he'd been promoted to Biloxi."], ["RICO", "Promoted to Biloxi? Marlow, that's not a promotion, that's a punishment with a river view."]],
	"city3_arrive": [["RICO", "Biloxi, home of Hard Rok, where the guitars are loud, the humidity is louder, and the whole place smells like a wet rock concert."], ["MARLOW", "Stay quiet in there, Rico, Hard Rok keeps its toughest guys by the stage, and they're very sensitive about their eardrums."], ["RICO", "Quiet's never been my strong suit, Marlow, you know that, I once got thrown out of a library for whispering too loudly."], ["MARLOW", "Rico, before you go in, I have to tell you something, and I need you not to throw anything, I'm the one who got James his seat at The House's table."], ["RICO", "...You WHAT."], ["MARLOW", "I thought he'd win, Rico, he always won, it was a safe bet, on paper, and I'd like to point out that the paper is currently on fire."], ["RICO", "I'm going to find you when this is over, Marlow, and I'm going to be so mad, I'm going to schedule it."], ["MARLOW", "That's fair, but I'm the only one who knows the way up to the penthouse, so climb first, yell second, and please hurry, I'm very uncomfortable."]],
	"city4_arrive": [["RICO", "Fremont, Old Vegas, where the neon is older than my debt and still glowing, which is more than I can say for my career."], ["MARLOW", "Goldun Nugget has a shark tank and a long memory, Rico, and everyone is welcome to come in, which is a real problem for the people who try to leave."], ["MAGS", "Rico, sweetie, I just wanted to remind you I'm still waiting at the top with a calculator, and I've added interest to the interest."], ["RICO", "Wait, what's that, a note, in James's handwriting? 'Don't come for me. I'm finally winning.'"], ["RICO", "He doesn't want to be saved, he's hooked, exactly like me, and I'd call that heartbreaking, but honestly, it's a little relatable."]],
	"city5_arrive": [["RICO", "The Strip, the nicest casino in the world, and I'm standing in it covered in alley, which is a bold look, and nobody has stopped me."], ["SILAS", "Dear boy, the cloak room is that way, we shall see what we can do, but I make no promises about the smell, or about your dignity."], ["THE HOUSE", "Welcome, Rico, we've been expecting you for years, and your brother has been dealing since lunch, he's doing wonderfully, and he asked about you twice."], ["MARLOW", "The penthouse is at the top of the Bellagiro, Rico, that's where James is, and please remember the plan, which is, do not bet him."]],
	"city1_clue": [["RICO", "An IOU in James's handwriting, 'I owe the House one brother,' and I'd say that's a typo, but it isn't, and that's the problem."], ["MARLOW", "Flip it over, there's a note on the back that says 'Reno,' so good news, Rico, James is alive, and bad news, he's in Reno."]],
	"city2_clue": [["RICO", "Another IOU, and this one says 'Dealing at Hard Rok,' so James isn't just gambling anymore, he's an employee of The House."], ["MARLOW", "Confirmed, James is dealing for The House now, fast hands, no sleep, and a vacant stare, it's honestly a very James career."]],
	"city3_clue": [["RICO", "An IOU and a torn receipt that says 'Fremont, Goldun Nugget, sublet: one lifetime,' and I'm not even going to ask how much that costs."], ["MARLOW", "He's moving up, Rico, every city gets him a better table, and every table gets him a worse deal, so I'd hurry."]],
	"city4_clue": [["RICO", "A chip with 'JAMES, PENTHOUSE' carved into it, which is either a clue or a very specific Christmas gift."], ["MARLOW", "That's the top floor of the Bellagiro, Rico, one more climb, and please don't die, I'd like to yell at you in person."]],
	"secret_found": [["RICO", "A hidden room with a secret table, and honestly, the House having a secret is the least surprising thing that's happened today."], ["MARLOW", "That's not on the map, Rico, so be careful in there, and by careful I mean reckless, because it's a secret table and you'll want the story."]],
	"secret_defeat": [["RICO", "Another secret table beaten, another stack of chips, and I think I'm starting to see why the House hid these."], ["MARLOW", "You're not supposed to know about those rooms, Rico, and the House is going to be very upset, in its calm, corporate way."], ["RICO", "Good, I'd hate to be the only one who's upset."]],
	"final_prelude": [["THE HOUSE", "You climbed my five cities, beat my table lords, and wore my clothes, Rico, and I must say, you have exceeded all my expectations, which were very low."], ["RICO", "And I still have a bet on you, so deal."], ["THE HOUSE", "Then sit, we shall play Texas Hold'em, and the pot, Rico, is your brother."]],
}
